overstatement across a 6-fold range of transmit power: 5.95 to 7.13 dB (mean 6.55 dB)
  The gap varies by 1.18 dB across that range and
  decreases monotonically with P_t: raising the transmit power moves the
  link towards the shot-noise limit, where SNR grows as P_t rather than
  P_t^2, so a fixed ratio of received powers maps to a smaller dB gap.
  The overstatement is therefore a property of the reflection model, not
  an artefact of the calibrated P_t -- it is present, and of the same
  order, at every power tested.

