   Their p.6 claim is that ambient adds ~0.49 dB and leaves >4.5 dB
   of margin. Their own 0.12 uW figure implies I_bg = 0.065 uA, which
   costs essentially nothing -- so the claim is self-consistent but
   rests on an ambient level ~10,000x below the value standard VLC
   noise models assume (740 uA). Which is right depends on the optical
   bandpass filter, which the paper does not specify. Report the sweep.

