  The overstatement grows with array size up to a point: the cosine
  model lets every mirror contribute whatever its orientation, so its
  gain scales with K more favourably than specular reflection allows.
  The gap peaks near K = 256 and then declines, as the reflected path
  comes to dominate the direct one in both arms. Extrapolations made
  under the cosine model are optimistic by about the plateau, not by
  a margin that keeps growing.

