Divergence in SNR dB against the gain divergence Delta_H.
Delta_H = 20 log10(H_cos / H_spec), free of the noise regime.
(The optical power ratio is 10 log10 of the same quantity, half of this.)
Diagnostic settings: uniform positions, face-up detector, no diffuse.

     K   SNR div    Delta_H   ratio   IRS/LoS
    36    3.12 dB     3.28 dB    0.95       0.3
   144    5.35 dB     5.90 dB    0.91       1.0
   400    6.32 dB     7.51 dB    0.84       2.8
   784    6.44 dB     8.24 dB    0.78       5.3
  1600    6.25 dB     8.75 dB    0.71      10.8

SNR ~ H^2 when thermal noise dominates, so the SNR divergence
equals Delta_H there; SNR ~ H when shot noise dominates, so it
falls to Delta_H / 2. The ratio column is therefore 1.0 at the
thermal limit and 0.5 at the shot limit. Delta_H rising while the
SNR divergence falls is the link moving between the two.
